<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">An increase in the number of Units offered by
500,000 Units to 5,979,452 Units (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $8.7 million) would increase cash, total stockholders&rsquo;
equity, and total capitalization on a pro forma as adjusted basis by approximately $679,000 from the amounts presented in the table above,
assuming the assumed offering price of $1.46 per Unit remains the same, and after deducting underwriting discounts and commissions and
estimated offering expenses payable by us.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">A decrease in the number of Units offered by500,000
Units to 4,979,452 Units (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $7.3 million) would decrease cash, total stockholders&rsquo; equity,
and total capitalization on a pro forma as adjusted basis by approximately $679,000 from the amounts presented in the table above, assuming
the assumed offering price of $1.46 per Unit remains the same, and after deducting underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated
offering expenses payable by us.</P>
<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">A $0.25 increase in the assumed initial public
offering price to $1.71 per share (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $9.4 million) would increase cash, total stockholders&rsquo;
equity, and total capitalization on a pro forma as adjusted basis by approximately $1.3 million from the amounts presented in the table
above, assuming that the number of Units offered by us, as set forth on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting
the estimated underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses payable by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">A $0.25 decrease in the assumed initial public offering price to $1.21
per share (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $6.6 million) would decrease cash, total stockholders&rsquo; equity, and total
capitalization on a pro forma as adjusted basis by approximately $1.3 million from the amounts presented in the table above, assuming
that the number of Units offered by us, as set forth on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting the estimated
underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses payable by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
pro forma as adjusted information discussed above is illustrative only and will be adjusted based on the actual public offering price
and other terms of this offering determined at pricing.</FONT></P>

