<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">An increase in the number of Units offered by
500,000 Units to 5,979,452 Units (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $8.7 million) would increase our pro forma as adjusted
net tangible book value as of June 30, 2023 after this offering to $13,198,618, or approximately $0.83 per share , and would change the
dilution to investors in this offering to approximately $0.63 per share, assuming that the assumed offering price per share, as set forth
on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting the estimated underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses
payable by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">A decrease in the number of Units offered by 500,000
Units to 4,979,452 Units (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $7.3 million) would decrease our pro forma as adjusted net tangible
book value as of June 30, 2023 after this offering to $11,840,818, or approximately $0.79 per share, and would change the dilution to
investors in this offering to approximately $0.67 per share, assuming that the assumed offering price per share, as set forth on the cover
page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting the estimated underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses payable
by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">A $0.25 increase in the assumed initial public
offering price to $1.71 per share (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $9.4 million) would increase our pro forma as adjusted
net tangible book value as of June 30, 2023 after this offering to $13,793,691, or approximately $0.89 per share, and would change the
dilution to investors in this offering to approximately $0.57 per share, assuming that the number of Units offered by us, as set forth
on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting the estimated underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses
payable by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">A $0.25 decrease in the assumed initial public
offering price to $1.21 per share (resulting in gross proceeds of approximately $6.6 million) would decrease our pro forma as adjusted
net tangible book value as of June 30, 2023 after this offering to $11,245,745, or approximately $0.73 per share, and would change the
dilution to investors in this offering to approximately $0.73 per share, assuming that the number of Units offered by us, as set forth
on the cover page of this prospectus, remains the same, after deducting the estimated underwriting discount and estimated offering expenses
payable by us.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The dilution information discussed above is illustrative
only and may change based on the actual public offering price and other terms of this offering.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The dilution table above is based on the number
of shares outstanding as of June 30, 2023, and excludes:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

